{"id": "38711", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=38711", "title": "Wayne (Michigan)", "text": "Wayne is a city in Wayne County in the state of Michigan."}
{"id": "38712", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=38712", "title": "Wayne (New Jersey)", "text": "Wayne is a city in New Jersey and home of William Paterson University.\nGet in.\nYou can drive a car or take the bus. Three NJ Transit lines run through this pickle of a town: the 197, the 744 and 748, with some others heading to Willowbrook but not serving further reaches of the town. Schedules and fares can be obtained on NJ Transit's website[dead link]. The trip from Manhattan by bus takes about an hour to 1 1/4 hours."}
{"id": "38713", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=38713", "title": "Wayne (Pennsylvania)", "text": "Wayne is in Delaware County, Pennsylvania.\nUnderstand.\nOriginally, a small quaker town in the early 1600s, Wayne has become a bustling community in the heart of the Main Line. Started as a rural farming community, over time affluent families moved to the area.\nGet around.\nEverything in Wayne is accessible by only a short walk. A car is not a necessity to see and do things here. If needed public buses, and the Septa train station are only a short distance away. \nBuy.\nWayne is filled with quaint and unique shops. New stores are always popping up. From trendy baby stores, to sophisticated shopping, there is something for everyone. A few popular stores are Genes, Wayne Sporting Goods, South Moon Under, Anthropologie, The Pink Turtle and Wayne Jewelers.\nEat.\nNo matter what your taste, there is a place for everyone to eat here. Local favorites are Christopher's, The Great American Pub, and Minellas Diner. And in case you have a sweet tooth, there are plenty of bakeries in the area such as Aux Petites Delices and Great Harvest Bread.\nSleep.\nFor lodging purposes, the Wayne Hotel, the Courtyard Marriot and the Valley Forge Suites."}
